$add_video_embedding_files — write per-fragment .ahvemb sidecars next to source videos

SUMMARY
  For each videos[] file: detect scene fragments in memory (same as $split_video_fast,
  ffmpeg-scaled frame hashes at width=320, without writing MP4s), sample every Nth
  frame per fragment, average SigLIP 2 embeddings, and write `.ahvemb/<video>.ahvemb`
  in the same folder as the source file.

SYNTAX
  $add_video_embedding_files
  $add_video_embedding_files(every=500)
  $add_video_embedding_files(threshold=10, min_frames=100, gpu=True)
  $add_video_embedding_files(overwrite=True)

INPUT
  videos[] — source video files (typically source_path=True from $folder)

OUTPUT
  Pass-through — input bundle unchanged. Sidecar files on disk only.

SIDEcar FORMAT (.ahvemb)
  One line per fragment, space-separated:
    start_frame end_frame base64_embedding

  start_frame — 0-based inclusive (same as $split_video labels)
  end_frame   — 0-based exclusive
  base64_embedding — 256-d float16 SigLIP vector (same as $video2embedding)

ARGUMENTS
  samples=   — random frame images kept per fragment during scan (default 5)
               merged fragments shuffle combined pools and keep samples=
  every=     — optional override: sample every Nth frame instead of random
  threshold=   — scene-change hash diff (default 10, from $split_video_fast)
  hash_size=   — per-frame hash size (default 8)
  min_frames=  — merge short fragments (default 100)
  width=       — ffmpeg scale width for hash frames (default 320)
  model=       — default | 224 | base-224 (same as $image2embedding)
  gpu=         — use CUDA when available
  overwrite=   — rewrite .ahvemb even if it already exists (default: skip)

DEPENDENCIES
  Uses .venvs/media (ffmpeg, imagehash, torch, transformers).
  Run tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1 once, or: uv sync --extra media --extra split_video_fast

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_ADD_VIDEO_EMBEDDING_FILES=1 — real fragment detection, placeholder embeddings.
  AH_ADD_VIDEO_EMBEDDING_FILES_GPU=0     — force CPU.

EXAMPLE
  @all_videos: $folder('test_data', '*.mp4', subfolders=True, source_path=True)
  @create_emb: @all_videos -> $add_video_embedding_files

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — videos[] pass through unchanged.
